---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="ShibusenRO"
  subtitle="A full-stack game platform combining a modern web application, legacy MMORPG infrastructure, payments, shared identity and custom client tooling."
  eyebrow="Personal Project · Case Study"
  stack={['Laravel', 'Docker', 'MariaDB', 'C#', 'Oracle Cloud', 'Cloudflare', 'rAthena']}
>
  <div class="case-grid">
    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        ShibusenRO started as an independent learning project: connect an online game server
        with a modern web platform and make both systems behave as a single product.
      </p>
      <p>
        The result combines account management, game data, payments, in-game currency,
        a web shop, cloud infrastructure, a custom launcher and update tooling.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Architecture</h2>
      <p>
        The platform runs on Oracle Cloud ARM64 using Docker Compose. rAthena login, char
        and map processes are separated into independent services, alongside Laravel web
        applications and MariaDB. Caddy and Cloudflare handle the public web layer.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Integration</h2>
      <p>
        A dedicated Laravel service layer integrates directly with the legacy game schema.
        Web accounts, characters, rankings and the in-game cash balance are based on the
        real rAthena data model rather than a disconnected copy.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Payments & Transactions</h2>
      <p>
        Mercado Pago integration includes order creation, signed webhook validation,
        idempotent crediting and transactional shop purchases designed to avoid duplicate
        charges or partial item delivery.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Client Tooling</h2>
      <p>
        A custom Windows launcher built with C#/.NET manages client versions, file manifests,
        patching and a separate updater capable of updating the launcher itself.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Operations</h2>
      <p>
        The project includes Linux administration, firewall rules, Cloudflare/DNS,
        container networking, backups with integrity checks and automated community tooling.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</CaseStudyLayout>
